                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Feels more like a walking simulator than a full survival game. The map is large and the terrain looks good, but there is basically only one biome, so exploration starts feeling repetitive fast. Enemy variety is limited too. You will mostly run into a handful of zombie types and a few hostile animals, and they all behave pretty similarly.\r\n\r\nThe story is actually pretty interesting and the collectible notes are a nice touch, but the ending feels rushed. Weather effects can get frustrating since heavy fog or storms make it almost impossible to see, and they even carry into cutscenes, which ruins the atmosphere.\r\n\r\nMost structures can be entered, but there is not much to do inside besides grabbing a chest or fighting the occasional enemy. Hitboxes are also inconsistent, which makes combat feel clunky.\r\n\r\nOverall, I would give it a 4/10. If you really want to spend around 20 hours and ten dollars on the regular survival mode, you can, but in my opinion it is not worth the time or money.",
